 "text": "Hey, how are you holding up? Totally understandable. At home, those little breaks can build up fast. Think of it like a commute. Taking a short walk or a coffee break at regular intervals keeps exhaustion at bay. Lots of small things count. Straightening at desk, stretching, taking a deep breath. Something simple that reminds you to stay alert and healthy. Exactly. Leave it in the room for now and come out it for the short break. It helps make it feel like a proper break. Enjoy it, and start each break with a few deep breaths. Sounds good. Lots of light so far.",
